
Typical environment needs:

    $ export PATH="/opt/logicblox/lb-steve-client/bin:/opt/logicblox/lb-steve-frontend/bin:/opt/logicblox/lb-steve-worker/bin:$PATH"
    $ export AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID="..."
    $ export AWS_SECRET_KEY="..."

To start the front-end:

    $ lb-steve-frontend --config ./custom.config

where custom.config is for example:

    ----------------------------------
    tmpdir = /tmp

    [job-queue]
    sqs_queue_url = https://sqs.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/297794765570/martin-steve-jobs

    [status-queue]
    sqs_queue_url = https://sqs.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/297794765570/martin-steve-jobs-status
    ----------------------------------

To start a worker:

    $ export NIX_PATH=worker=$PWD/worker-minimal:$NIX_PATH
    $ lb-steve-worker --incoming https://sqs.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/297794765570/martin-steve-jobs \
                      --outgoing https://sqs.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/297794765570/martin-steve-jobs-status

To upload a job implementation:

    $ lb-steve-client upload-impl --impl total-v1 -i ~/total.tar.gz


Running jobs
------------

    To run a job:

        $ lb-steve-client create-job --impl total-v1 -i input.txt -o output.txt

    To run a job while keeping results in S3:

        $ lb-steve-client create-job --impl total-v1 -i s3://bucket/data.txt -o s3://bucket/output

    The input/output can be mixed between S3 and local files:

        $ lb-steve-client create-job --impl total-v1 -i input.txt -o s3://bucket/output
        $ lb-steve-client create-job --impl total-v1 -i s3://bucket/data.txt -o output.txt

    Diretories can also be used as input and output:

        $ lb-steve-client create-job --impl total-v1 -i input-dir -o output-dir

